# SCHLAR — PROMPT 6: ACCOUNTANT / FEE MANAGER AND HR / STAFF MANAGER

## 1. PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Continue building the existing SCHLAR School Management System frontend demo.

Implement two complete, professionally designed, interactive role workspaces:

1. Accountant / Fee Manager
2. HR / Staff Manager

This is Prompt 6 of the existing 12-prompt SCHLAR implementation roadmap.

The objective is to demonstrate realistic school financial administration and human-resource management using coherent data, functional workflows, meaningful validation, appropriate permissions, and consistent navigation.

**Do not restart the project, replace the architecture, or rebuild unrelated modules.**

First inspect the current codebase and the work completed in Prompts 1–5. Reuse the existing application shell, centralized role configuration, permissions, theme system, routing, state management, data models, reusable components, and persistence mechanisms.

Do not assume previous prompts were implemented perfectly. Verify what exists, identify missing functionality, and extend it carefully.

The product principle remains:

"Simple enough for a first-time user, powerful enough for a real school."

Simplify workflows and navigation, not capabilities, data integrity, or security boundaries.

This remains a frontend demonstration. Implement genuine frontend interactions using the existing application state. Never claim that the application has a production database, backend security, real payroll processing, actual bank integration, or cross-device synchronization unless those capabilities genuinely exist.

